  "name": "Wan 2.2 — key-frame animation (4 frames to video)",
  "description": "Turn four still key frames into one continuous video. Wan 2.2 generates a smooth animated transition between each consecutive pair of frames (frame 1→2, 2→3, 3→4) and stitches the three segments into a single clip that passes through all four images in order. Optionally describe the motion for each transition; leave a box empty to just morph between those two frames. Runs the fast 4-step Lightning path at 720×720.\n\nTip: use frames that share the same subject and framing so the transitions stay coherent.",
